   "html_text": "Dworkin’s idea of constructive interpretation plays a key role in his explanation of the normative ground and content of these associative obligations. In the case of political communities, the interpretive target is the community’s past political decisions – roughly speaking, the decisions made and enforced by the community’s political institutions, such as legislatures, executive agencies, and courts. In this context, constructive interpretation seeks to adduce principles of justice, fairness,",
